  luma_power_y float8 [not null, default: 1, note: 'Per-channel power applied to the normalized RGB signal. Varying: may carry time samples (animatable). (y); source: float3 backPlate:<instanceName>:luma:power']
  luma_power_z float8 [not null, default: 1, note: 'Per-channel power applied to the normalized RGB signal. Varying: may carry time samples (animatable). (z); source: float3 backPlate:<instanceName>:luma:power']
  plate_visibility text [not null, default: 'solo', note: 'Toggles the visibility of the back plate to all cameras, only the owning camera, or no cameras. Varying: may carry time samples (animatable).; source: token backPlate:<instanceName>:plateVisibility']
  Note: 'BackPlateAPI: This schema specifies a back plate i.e. a camera-constrained but not always camera-facing texture card, that exists in scene space. Multiple back plates can be applied to a single camera and each plate can independently specify its own overall visibility, as well as its own opacity and depth varying over the plate.'
